    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and it meets all four requirements. `pytest -q` passes (1 test). I also ran a check where a stub transport returned a 500 on every request: the client made 3 attempts (the original plus 2 retries), and each one was logged as `INFO:app.http:GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models`.\n\nI didn't add or install anything. The installed openai 3.19.2 uses a library called `httpx2` rather than `httpx`, so the function builds an `httpx2.Client` with the stub `transport` and a request event hook, then passes it to `OpenAI` with `max_retries=2`. The hook runs once per attempt, which is why retries are logged.\n\nOne thing to know: the timeout (5 s connect, 30 s read/write/pool) is set on both the HTTP client and the `OpenAI` object. The SDK sends its own timeout with every request, which overrides the HTTP client's. If you set it only on the HTTP client, the SDK's defaults would quietly apply instead. The check confirmed each request carried the correct values.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** I couldn't delete my temporary check script `_check.py` in the project root because removing it needed approval. You can delete it yourself, or tell me to go ahead."
